         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from San Jose CR Jade\n\nThese images are copyright for San Jose CR Jade and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"cr0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('cr0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Ceramic vessels. Photograph taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the Jade Museum in Costa Rica (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Physics: Always present - many times we are so focused on ourselves or on opposites that we do not notice what is always present. (<htcite1>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMayaCRJade\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMayaCRJade', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Maya text. Photo taken on <htdate1>, during a visit to the Museum of Jade in San José, Costa Rica (<htcite2>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Playing with Consonants and Vowels - An interactive game to understand how syllables are created. (<htcite3>)</li><li>Multiplying the Findings - an educational game in which the reader visualizes multiplication while exploring different archaeological sites. (<htcite4>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part I) - In this first stage, learning is reinforced by completing number sequences that go up to the hundreds, helping to consolidate the understanding of basic foundations. (<htcite5>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part II) - Continuing the challenge, this stage presents sequences that extend up to the billions, deepening the mastery of numerical patterns. (<htcite6>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
